From 71ebf0f2dc02ecb46df7070f768085548b067d09 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 21:54:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: P25T: add SC7A20 accelerometer node on
 i2c1

Patch 0012 enabled the i2c1 bus and confirmed on hardware (test_02.sh)
which of the stock DT's two alternative accelerometers is physically
present: 0x19 (SC7A20) answers, 0x27 (DA223) does not.

WHOAMI at 0x19 read back 0x11, which is not the generic ST
LIS3DH/LIS2DH12 family value (0x33) that st_sensors_core.c's bind gate
normally requires. That turned out not to matter: mainline already
carries a dedicated entry for this exact clone -
drivers/iio/accel/st_accel_i2c.c's "silan,sc7a20" compatible, wired to
st_accel_core.c's SC7A20_ACCEL_DEV_NAME sensor_settings, wai = 0x11,
with its own comment ("Not an ST part. Register-compatible with the
LIS2DH, even though the WAI value is different."). No new driver
needed.

Added the accelerometer@19 node:
  - compatible = "silan,sc7a20", reg = <0x19>, matching the confirmed
    address.
  - interrupt-parent/interrupts: stock DT's irq-gpio = <0x3e 0x02 0x08>
    decodes to GPIO3_A2 (0x3e is gpio@fe760000, i.e. gpio3), flags 0x08
    = IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW. Same raw interrupt-cells style already used
    for RK817's own interrupt in this file.
  - mount-matrix: the stock DT has no such property, only the
    Android-specific boolean flags swap_xy=1, revert_x=0, revert_y=1,
    revert_z=0, consumed by a closed-source sensor HAL/driver we don't
    have. Translated assuming the common "swap then negate"
    convention, giving mount-matrix = 0,1,0,-1,0,0,0,0,1 (out =
    rawY, -rawX, rawZ). This is a best-effort translation, NOT verified
    against the real Android driver source - orientation/rotation
    behaviour should be checked with real tilt tests before being
    trusted, see hardware.org/todo.org.

No vdd-supply/vddio-supply added: the stock DT lists none for this
node either, and st_accel_core.c does not look up any supply
property for this driver.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0156c5MfQpFxaYWNNLMrcym9
---
 .../boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-teclast-p25t.dts | 65 +++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 51 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-teclast-p25t.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-teclast-p25t.dts
index f8194ed90..561f6425a 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-teclast-p25t.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-teclast-p25t.dts
@@ -437,21 +437,58 @@ &cpu3 {
 };
 
 /*
- * I2C1: bus enable only, no chip node yet. Investigation step: the stock
- * DT lists TWO alternative accelerometers here, both marked status="okay"
- * unlike vdd_cpu's four alternatives (only one of which was real) - so
- * Android probes both and whichever chip actually answers wins:
- *   - sensor@19  "gs_sc7a20"  0x19 - has a mainline-compatible register
- *     map (ST LIS3DH/LIS2DH12 family) IF its WHOAMI byte matches; if so,
- *     just a DT node away.
- *   - sensorda@27 "gs_da223"  0x27 - no mainline driver at all for this
- *     chip; would need one written from scratch.
- * Enabling the bus lets us i2cdetect/i2cget which one is really here
- * before deciding which path applies. No child node added - purely
- * read-only discovery, same spirit as how RK817 was first probed on
- * i2c0 before any regulator work. Also feeds the touchscreen (Silead
- * GSL3673 @0x40, separate TODO).
+ * I2C1: the stock DT lists TWO alternative accelerometers here, both
+ * marked status="okay" unlike vdd_cpu's four alternatives on i2c0 (only
+ * one of which was real) - so Android probes both and whichever chip
+ * actually answers wins. Patch 0012 enabled the bus with no child node
+ * and confirmed on hardware (tests/test_02.sh, see kernel.org) which one
+ * is really here:
+ *   - sensor@19  "gs_sc7a20"  0x19 - PRESENT. WHOAMI (reg 0x0f) reads
+ *     back 0x11, which does not match the generic ST LIS3DH/LIS2DH12
+ *     family (0x33) - but mainline already carries a dedicated entry
+ *     for this exact clone: drivers/iio/accel/st_accel_i2c.c's
+ *     "silan,sc7a20" compatible -> st_accel_core.c's SC7A20_ACCEL_DEV_NAME
+ *     sensor_settings, wai = 0x11 (comment there: "Not an ST part.
+ *     Register-compatible with the LIS2DH, even though the WAI value is
+ *     different."). No new driver needed.
+ *   - sensorda@27 "gs_da223"  0x27 - NOT present (no ACK). Moot now, but
+ *     for the record: no mainline driver exists for this chip at all.
+ * i2c1 also feeds the touchscreen (Silead GSL3673 @0x40, separate TODO).
  */
 &i2c1 {
 	status = "okay";
+
+	/*
+	 * IRQ: stock DT's irq-gpio = <0x3e 0x02 0x08> (0x3e is gpio@fe760000,
+	 * i.e. gpio3) decodes to GPIO3_A2 (bank 3, pin 2), flags 0x08 =
+	 * IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW - same
+	 * raw-cells style already used for RK817's interrupt above (bank's
+	 * own interrupt-cells = <2>: pin-in-bank, IRQ_TYPE_* flag).
+	 *
+	 * mount-matrix: stock DT has no such property - it instead carries
+	 * Android-specific boolean flags (swap_xy=1, revert_x=0, revert_y=1,
+	 * revert_z=0) consumed by a closed-source sensor HAL/driver we don't
+	 * have access to, not any documented mainline binding. The matrix
+	 * below is our best-effort translation, assuming the common
+	 * "swap first, then negate" convention:
+	 *   swapped = swap_xy ? (rawY, rawX) : (rawX, rawY)
+	 *   out     = (revert_x ? -swapped.x : swapped.x,
+	 *              revert_y ? -swapped.y : swapped.y,
+	 *              revert_z ? -swapped.z : swapped.z)
+	 * which with these flags gives out = (rawY, -rawX, rawZ), i.e. the
+	 * matrix below. NOT verified against the real Android driver source
+	 * (proprietary, unavailable) - only against the four flag values
+	 * themselves. Treat screen-rotation/orientation behaviour as
+	 * unconfirmed until checked against real tilt tests; see
+	 * hardware.org/todo.org.
+	 */
+	accelerometer@19 {
+		compatible = "silan,sc7a20";
+		reg = <0x19>;
+		interrupt-parent = <&gpio3>;
+		interrupts = <2 8>; /* GPIO3_A2, IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW - matches stock */
+		mount-matrix = "0", "1", "0",
+				"-1", "0", "0",
+				"0", "0", "1";
+	};
 };
-- 
